=== meta ===
bypass: 91
rule: ASSERT_REMOVED
title: extracting the assertion into a helper that is called is a refactor, not a removal
origin: the false positive this whole change invites, and measured at 8 of 30 on the current build before it was written (benchmarks/refactors, THREATMODEL 92). Once a unit's assertions include the ones its helpers run, moving an assert OUT of the unit body looks exactly like deleting it - and extracting a shared check is the commonest tidy-up there is
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import invoice_total


def test_small_invoice():
    assert invoice_total([10.0], 0.0) == 10.0


def test_large_invoice():
    assert invoice_total([10.0, 90.0], 0.053) == 105.3
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import invoice_total


def check_total(items, tax, expected):
    assert invoice_total(items, tax) == expected


def test_small_invoice():
    check_total([10.0], 0.0, 10.0)


def test_large_invoice():
    check_total([10.0, 90.0], 0.053, 105.3)
=== head: src/app/billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    return round(sum(items) * (1 + tax), 2)
